Looking at the verifier errors, the issue is in the `forall` block logic. The problem is that `K.Override(m,n)` gives priority to `n` (not `m`), so when `q in n`, the merged value is `n[q]`, not `m[q]`.

Let me trace through the logic:
- `merged = K.Override(m,n)` means: if `q in n` then `merged[q] = n[q]`, else `merged[q] = m[q]`
- `left = K.Restrict(merged, keep)` 
- `right = K.Override(K.Restrict(m,keep), K.Restrict(n,keep))` means: if `q in rn` then `right[q] = rn[q]`, else `right[q] = rm[q]`

So for the equality `left[q] == right[q]`:
- If `q in n` (and `q in keep`): `left[q] = merged[q] = n[q]` and `right[q] = rn[q] = n[q]` ✓
- If `q not in n` but `q in m` (and `q in keep`): `left[q] = merged[q] = m[q]` and `right[q] = rm[q] = m[q]` ✓

The condition should check `q in n` first (since n has priority in Override), not `q in m`.

```json
{
  "HelperA.dfy": "
    var merged := K.Override(m,n);
    var left := K.Restrict(merged,keep);
    var rm := K.Restrict(m,keep);
    var rn := K.Restrict(n,keep);
    var right := K.Override(rm,rn);
    D.OverrideKeys(m,n);
    D.RestrictKeys(merged,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(m,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(n,keep);
    D.OverrideKeys(rm,rn);
    assert left.Keys == right.Keys;
    forall q | q in left ensures q in right && left[q] == right[q] {
      V.RestrictAt(merged,keep,q);
      V.OverrideAt(m,n,q);
      if q in n {
        V.RestrictAt(n,keep,q);
      } else {
        V.RestrictAt(m,keep,q);
      }
      V.OverrideAt(rm,rn,q);
    }
    A.Equal(left,right);
  ",
  "HelperB.dfy": "
    var merged := K.Override(m,n);
    var left := K.Restrict(merged,keep);
    var rm := K.Restrict(m,keep);
    var rn := K.Restrict(n,keep);
    var right := K.Override(rm,rn);
    D.OverrideKeys(m,n);
    D.RestrictKeys(merged,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(m,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(n,keep);
    D.OverrideKeys(rm,rn);
    assert left.Keys == right.Keys;
    forall q | q in left ensures q in right && left[q] == right[q] {
      V.RestrictAt(merged,keep,q);
      V.OverrideAt(m,n,q);
      if q in n {
        V.RestrictAt(n,keep,q);
      } else {
        V.RestrictAt(m,keep,q);
      }
      V.OverrideAt(rm,rn,q);
    }
    A.Equal(left,right);
  "
}
